RELATION TO HOMEOSTATIC RL
A reduction in internal drive/stress can:
organize useful behavior.

H88 adds an important engineering warning:

HOMEOSTATIC REWARD
IS STILL A REWARD CHANNEL.

It can be:
masked,
shifted,
confounded,
or
corrupted.

Therefore:
endogenous reward
does not automatically solve:
Goodhart / reward-hacking problems.

RELATION TO H51 / S7
H51:
functional consequence needs:
matched control
under passive confounding.

S7:
outcome correlation
is not:
causal value of information.

H88:
homeostatic improvement
is not:
causal functional value

unless:
action contribution is separated from:
waiting,
disturbance,
and
proxy corruption.

GENERAL PRINCIPLE
TARGET-FREE
SHOULD NOT MEAN:

UNCRITICALLY OPTIMIZE
WHATEVER INTERNAL SENSOR
HAPPENS TO GO DOWN.

A stronger formulation is:

CREDIT ACTIONS
FOR
PERSISTENT,
CAUSALLY ATTRIBUTABLE,
MULTI-CONSEQUENCE
RESTORATION
OF ORGANISM VIABILITY.

And:

WITHHOLD CONFIDENCE
WHEN
THE CONSEQUENCE CHANNELS
SHARE FAILURE PROVENANCE.

DECISION
AR-H88 is POSITIVE
for:
persistent matched multi-consequence causal credit

WITH A HARD COMMON-MODE SENSOR-CORRUPTION LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- immediate stress reduction is highly gameable;
- local improvement can hide exported harm;
- activity is not functional value;
- raw persistence is confounded by natural recovery;
- single persistent sensors can be hacked;
- typed independent viability proxies reduce single-channel gaming;
- matched controls remove waiting/passive-recovery credit;
- persistent multi-proxy credit can steer learning toward the genuinely restorative pathway;
- local causal scope must include downstream consequences when actions export burden;
- common-mode corruption defeats the tested multi-proxy causal stack.

Not demonstrated:

- a real target-free Yggdrasil viability variable;
- real action-decupled controls;
- real independent failure provenance;
- cognition from homeostatic credit;
- long-horizon semantic usefulness;
- protection when every viability channel shares corruption.

NEXT HIGH-VALUE MOVE
AR-H89 — CONSERVATION-ANCHORED VIABILITY / HARD-TO-FAKE CONSEQUENCE

H88's hard failure is:
common-mode proxy corruption.

Question:

Can some endogenous consequence channels be anchored to:
CONSERVATION / CAPACITY CONSTRAINTS
that are harder to spoof than:
ordinary measurements?

Candidate anchors:

- conserved resource mass from H56-H57;
- unresolved structural debt;
- real active-capacity occupancy;
- successful downstream resource uptake;
- topology/connectivity loss;
- reversible challenge using physically separate control paths.

Compare:

A.
soft viability sensors only;

B.
soft sensors + conserved-resource anchors;

C.
one corrupted anchor;

D.
all soft sensors corrupted;

E.
action that improves sensors by:
discarding useful capacity;

F.
true repair.

Desired:

SENSOR STATE
can lie.

But:
a transformation should not receive full credit
unless:
harder-to-fake conserved consequences
also improve.

This is NOT a claim that conservation equals intelligence.

It is an attempt to make:
the endogenous credit channel
less gameable.

Do not execute STAB-18-R1 during this lane.

